#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119535 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a86c24c2-97c2-534e-9c03-9735b031bb23" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "5eca7964-4613-5fd6-b952-778886687830" :question/math-academy-id "e-4771" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 9 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of $l_{42} \\cdot u_{24}$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U$, as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 9 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 1R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & R_{4}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{4} + 2R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{4} \\mid:=R_{4} + (-2)R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, since $l_{42}=-2$ and $u_{24}=-3$, we get\n\n$$\nl_{42} \\cdot u_{24} = (-2) \\cdot (-3) =6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119536 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "0ec2663e-be00-560b-8d42-d0e1b1d023c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4772" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry $l_{31}$ in the matrix $L$?" :question/worked-solution "We want to make $0$ at the position $a_{{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}1}}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the ${\\color{blue}3}$rd row of $A$, and we add the ${\\color{red}1}$st row of $A$ multiplied by ${\\color{purple}-4}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -10\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry $l_{{\\color{blue}3}{\\color{red}1}}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to $R_1$, taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\nl_{31}=-({\\color{purple}-4})=4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119628 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c159d750-ab1f-538b-b8cc-ae66ef1ae414" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix U of an LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "763fad5f-7cb7-5ff3-a14e-e2849e90906a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8924" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of $u_{33}$ in the matrix $U$?" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 11 & -16 \\\\ 6 & -8 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + (-6)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 11 & -16 \\\\ 0 & 22 & -26\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-2)R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 11 & -16 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u_{33}=6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119629 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "b19414c3-443f-5075-a2db-f27eb3a7e936" :question/math-academy-id "e-8925" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & -12 \\\\ -4 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of $l_{31} \\cdot u_{23}$?" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U$, as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & -12 \\\\ -4 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + 3R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -4 & 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + 2R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 24 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=R_{3} + (-1)R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 24 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFinally, since $l_{31}=-2$ and $u_{23}=-9$, we get\n\n$$\nl_{31} \\cdot u_{23} = (-2) \\cdot (-9) =18\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1763cbaa-4b69-5f98-9181-666a159537b1" :answer/type {:db/ident